# @pantry-pal/frontend
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) and adjust.
#
# Vite exposes ONLY variables prefixed with `VITE_` to browser code. Unprefixed
# variables below are read by `vite.config.ts` at startup and stay server-side.

# Dev server port. `strictPort` is on, so startup fails rather than silently
# picking another port and breaking the backend's CORS allowlist.
PORT=3000

# Where the dev server proxies `/api` and `/socket.io`.
BACKEND_PORT=3001
# Set this to override the full origin (e.g. a deployed backend).
# VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Development identity, sent as the `x-dev-user-email` header and in the socket
# handshake. Honoured only while the backend runs with DEV_AUTH=true. Defaults to
# the owner of the test household that `pnpm db:seed` creates; an unknown email
# becomes a new user with an empty "Home" household.
# VITE_DEV_USER_EMAIL=owner@pantry-pal.test
